  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c73bcde73ca45b24c870219573f99a55, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The flower stall. Funeral lilies, mostly. I closed early to come home.
    midDaysAnswer: The stall. No flowers left. I arranged the empty buckets, then walked home.
    finalDaysAnswer: Where the stall used to be. I stood there a while. Then here.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The bakery on Lenina Street. Six years at the ovens.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My new flat. I moved to the block last week. Still unpacking.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Home. My husband walked me to the corner. Married many years now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. Procedures I remember. Other things I lose. That is not a symptom.
    midDaysAnswer: I lose small things. Keys. Days. I wait up. I feel fine.
    finalDaysAnswer: A little tired. I have been waiting a long time. That is all.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No. My memory is perfect. I have never lost a single thing.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: A stiff neck from the dress. I bought it Monday. Brand new.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. I am not waiting for anything. There is no wedding. Never was.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Most people do not ask about the dress. You are not supposed to.
    - There is a ceremony soon. I am told to stay ready. So I am.
    midDays:
    - I asked someone what day it was. It was not the day I thought.
    - I have waited quite a while. A little longer is nothing.
    finalDays:
    - Will it rain? The dress cannot get wet. It has been cleaned once.
    - I counted the days. I stopped when I lost count. It was high.
